WEBVTT

00:08.710 --> 00:10.880
I like lunch break.

00:11.880 --> 00:18.130
Although my invisibleness causes me countless
inconveniences in my daily life,

00:18.960 --> 00:23.540
I can eat lunch at my favorite spots without being seen.

00:24.830 --> 00:27.580
Now then, where should I eat today?

00:29.040 --> 00:31.000
Yesterday, I ate in the music classroom.

00:32.040 --> 00:33.750
The day before yesterday, I ate in the science lab.

00:35.210 --> 00:38.790
The weather is nice today,
so eating outside might be a good idea.

00:43.250 --> 00:45.880
I kinda enjoy this time of day.

00:51.920 --> 00:55.290
I can't help but feel like
I'm doing something a little naughty.

01:00.130 --> 01:02.380
Lunch break is like a mini adventure.

01:03.960 --> 01:07.880
There are places to sit all over this school.

01:09.460 --> 01:12.880
There are plenty of places to eat lunch.

01:16.000 --> 01:16.710
Umph.

01:19.040 --> 01:21.040
I guess I'll eat here today.

01:22.040 --> 01:24.380
Geez, I was looking for you!

01:26.880 --> 01:28.130
But today...

01:31.920 --> 01:33.750
Kubo-san found me once again.

01:35.920 --> 01:38.710
Please, just for a moment

01:38.710 --> 01:42.750
Let the time freeze

01:44.960 --> 01:48.380
When did it start?

01:48.380 --> 01:52.040
I cannot remember

01:52.880 --> 01:56.630
Who actually cares?

01:56.630 --> 01:59.380
"It doesn't matter"

01:59.920 --> 02:02.960
Laughing or shedding tears

02:02.960 --> 02:07.080
Whenever we realized

02:07.540 --> 02:13.040
Or too persistent to take in sometime

02:14.380 --> 02:24.290
Ready? And go as the traffic light changes (As we are)

02:24.290 --> 02:28.290
No words needed (as far as we can be)

02:28.460 --> 02:31.420
We can surely make it

02:31.420 --> 02:35.080
Even if it wasn't dramatic

02:35.250 --> 02:38.920
Even if it was boring and I was moaning

02:39.210 --> 02:44.130
I'll remember this day

02:44.580 --> 02:45.580
When? I don't know

02:46.130 --> 02:49.830
I don't need no romantic words

02:50.000 --> 02:53.420
I just want one thing

02:53.500 --> 02:56.170
Let the time freeze

02:56.170 --> 03:00.080
Just for a moment...

03:00.580 --> 03:02.500
The words fell

03:05.670 --> 03:10.290
<b>Episode 5: White Day and a Destination for Feelings</b>

03:05.790 --> 03:08.000
Kubo-san? Why are you here?

03:08.750 --> 03:10.670
Let's eat lunch together!

03:15.460 --> 03:16.790
Huh?

03:16.790 --> 03:18.880
But you always eat with your friends.

03:18.880 --> 03:22.960
Oh, Tama is at a committee meeting,
and Hazuki has a club meeting.

03:23.670 --> 03:24.710
Oh, okay.

03:24.920 --> 03:26.500
Yep, that's right.

03:39.250 --> 03:40.380
Aren't you going to eat?

03:40.790 --> 03:42.790
Oh! Yeah.

03:45.880 --> 03:46.960
Wow!

03:47.250 --> 03:50.000
Your bento looks delicious!

03:51.000 --> 03:56.210
Your rolled omelets and octopus sausages look so good!

04:00.460 --> 04:01.170
You...

04:02.000 --> 04:02.880
You wanna try some?

04:02.880 --> 04:04.380
Really, it's cool with you?

04:04.920 --> 04:05.670
Yeah.

04:06.460 --> 04:09.630
Alrighty! Then let's trade rolled omelets.

04:09.630 --> 04:12.080
Huh? No need for that.

04:13.960 --> 04:14.630
Here!

04:20.080 --> 04:21.000
Um.

04:21.630 --> 04:24.000
Hmm? Aren't you going to eat it?

04:26.040 --> 04:26.790
Thanks.

04:26.790 --> 04:27.420
Ah!

04:28.130 --> 04:29.330
That was a close shave.

04:31.420 --> 04:32.540
That's too bad.

04:33.040 --> 04:33.920
What is?

04:33.920 --> 04:36.250
Hmm, what indeed?

04:40.630 --> 04:42.000
Here, Kubo-san.

04:42.750 --> 04:43.710
Thanks.

05:01.790 --> 05:03.170
Mmm!

05:03.170 --> 05:06.290
Your rolled omelet is delish!

05:09.250 --> 05:10.170
What's the matter?

05:11.460 --> 05:14.290
Nothing, I'm just glad you enjoyed it.

05:15.330 --> 05:17.460
Try one of my rolled omelets too!

05:17.830 --> 05:18.790
It's great!

05:21.790 --> 05:23.960
Kubo-san's rolled omelet.

05:34.670 --> 05:35.630
It's really good!

05:35.630 --> 05:36.540
Right!

05:37.250 --> 05:38.830
I made them!

05:44.040 --> 05:44.790
No way.

05:46.380 --> 05:48.330
Well, I did fib.

05:52.580 --> 05:53.790
What's this?

05:55.670 --> 05:56.710
I get it.

05:57.130 --> 06:00.630
You wanted to eat my cooking.

06:01.130 --> 06:02.670
You could've just told me.

06:03.790 --> 06:04.920
I didn't say that.

06:06.170 --> 06:07.790
Guess my hands are tied.

06:08.880 --> 06:11.210
I'll make something and bring it next time.

06:12.580 --> 06:14.790
But I didn't ask you to.

06:15.330 --> 06:17.920
So let's eat lunch together again, m'kay?

06:27.080 --> 06:29.460
All right, whenever you feel like it.

06:30.040 --> 06:32.500
Stare.

06:32.710 --> 06:33.710
Kubo-san?

06:34.790 --> 06:36.210
Oh, my octopus!

06:37.790 --> 06:41.080
Hey, Shiraishi-kun, what sorts of food do you like?

06:43.130 --> 06:45.920
But more important than that, my octopus...

06:46.330 --> 06:48.080
What's your favorite food?

06:51.500 --> 06:52.960
Hamburger steak, I guess.

06:54.000 --> 06:54.960
Gotcha.

06:55.580 --> 06:57.170
Mine is stew!

06:58.380 --> 06:59.380
Oh, really?

07:00.130 --> 07:00.790
Yep.

07:01.920 --> 07:03.210
Go on, eat.

07:03.920 --> 07:04.880
Yeah.

07:06.210 --> 07:08.670
It's warmer than usual today, huh?

07:14.790 --> 07:20.130
Thinking about it, this might be the first time
I've seen someone else's bento.

07:21.920 --> 07:22.830
Yeah, it is.

07:23.960 --> 07:25.380
It's only natural.

07:26.000 --> 07:29.790
I've never eaten with someone else during lunch break.

07:31.750 --> 07:32.500
It's so good!

07:55.580 --> 07:58.710
Kubocchi, you've gotten so cute lately.

07:58.710 --> 08:02.750
I see what you mean. It's like she's glowing.

08:04.710 --> 08:06.330
What? That's out of left field.

08:06.330 --> 08:08.130
Do you have a crush?

08:07.080 --> 08:08.330
<b>Meow,</b>

08:07.080 --> 08:08.330
<b>hehe...</b>

08:10.040 --> 08:11.250
A crush?

08:12.330 --> 08:16.040
Oh, that's right. Nagisa has yet to fall in love.

08:16.040 --> 08:17.790
Huh? Really?

08:18.380 --> 08:20.290
She's still childlike.

08:21.960 --> 08:25.250
So that's why I got such a meh reaction from her.

08:26.130 --> 08:27.540
For me...

08:28.580 --> 08:30.540
My first love was my dad?!

08:31.330 --> 08:37.040
I'm dead serious, I wanted to marry my dad when
I was in first grade. What was wrong with me?

08:37.040 --> 08:38.580
That's a great story.

08:38.880 --> 08:41.250
I'm sure your dad would be delighted to hear that.

08:44.790 --> 08:47.250
You're blessed with a face like that
and still haven't had your first kiss?

08:47.460 --> 08:48.380
Can I steal it?

08:48.380 --> 08:49.830
Wait, what?!

08:49.830 --> 08:50.580
Oh?

08:50.580 --> 08:53.460
Anyway, back to the subject, Nagisa.

08:54.170 --> 08:58.920
Is there anyone you're interested in,
even if you're not crushing on them?

09:01.130 --> 09:02.830
Someone I'm interested in...

09:03.130 --> 09:08.080
Like, is there someone your eyes follow,
you end up thinking about them,

09:08.080 --> 09:11.000
and you want to talk to them a lot?

09:13.750 --> 09:14.500
Who?

09:19.210 --> 09:20.330
Shiraishi-kun.

09:21.250 --> 09:22.080
Shira...

09:24.420 --> 09:28.080
I find myself thinking about how far his invisibility goes.

09:29.080 --> 09:31.670
When I take my eyes off him, he's gone in a flash.

09:32.130 --> 09:36.000
Hmm, that sounds more like "like" than "love."

09:36.250 --> 09:37.080
Why?

09:37.080 --> 09:37.670
Huh?

09:39.460 --> 09:41.920
Why such a mid guy?

09:43.710 --> 09:47.790
He's not athletic, an honor student, or hot.

09:48.210 --> 09:49.210
So why?

09:51.790 --> 09:53.330
Tama, enough.

09:54.750 --> 09:58.790
That might be how the Shiraishi-kun you know seems...

10:12.080 --> 10:13.130
It's so good!

10:13.630 --> 10:18.040
But I know more of Shiraishi-kun's
strong points than you.

10:18.790 --> 10:21.380
I don't like it when people badmouth him.

10:21.830 --> 10:24.130
I didn't mean it like that!

10:24.130 --> 10:25.580
I know.

10:26.040 --> 10:27.830
I said that too harshly.

10:28.420 --> 10:31.170
Speaking of which, what are Shiraishi's strong points?

10:33.580 --> 10:35.330
Why do you ask?

10:35.330 --> 10:37.170
My interest is kind of piqued.

10:38.710 --> 10:39.500
That's confidential.

10:41.380 --> 10:44.670
You're super possessive of him, how unexpected!

10:44.670 --> 10:46.330
That's so not true!

10:46.750 --> 10:48.880
I don't own him or anything.

10:49.250 --> 10:53.000
Then how would you feel if you saw
Shiraishi talking to another girl?

10:54.290 --> 10:55.630
Shiraishi-kun...

10:56.630 --> 10:57.750
Talking to...

10:59.920 --> 11:01.920
Another girl?

11:03.130 --> 11:05.960
Could this be lo-

11:06.580 --> 11:07.830
Shhh!

11:08.130 --> 11:09.250
Why?

11:09.500 --> 11:11.580
Because it's her first.

11:11.960 --> 11:14.380
Let's just keep an eye on things until she figures it out.

11:15.290 --> 11:16.290
All right.

11:16.710 --> 11:19.830
Just like Kubocchi is possessive of Shiraishi,

11:20.130 --> 11:24.630
we should be possessive of
her cute face a little while longer.

11:24.630 --> 11:25.750
Agreed.

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>Let's go home</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>soon...</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>Uh,</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>sorry</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>One</b>

11:29.000 --> 11:33.000
<b>hour</b>

11:29.010 --> 11:33.000
<b>later</b>

11:38.880 --> 11:41.630
For some reason, I woke up ridiculously early today,

11:42.630 --> 11:46.670
so I felt like being the first one to get to class.

11:47.580 --> 11:51.080
Of course, I've never been the first to arrive before.

11:52.250 --> 11:56.040
No one will even notice if
I'm the first person to get to class,

11:56.500 --> 11:59.250
but it's fine with me if I'm the only one who knows.

12:03.210 --> 12:03.960
Oh.

12:05.960 --> 12:07.290
I'm the first one here.

12:09.790 --> 12:10.830
Too bad.

12:11.170 --> 12:13.130
I got here first.

12:15.420 --> 12:16.250
I lost?

12:16.750 --> 12:19.420
Morning, Shiraishi-kun. You got here early.

12:21.500 --> 12:23.380
So did you.

12:24.420 --> 12:27.790
For some reason, I wanted to be
the first one to get to class today.

12:29.790 --> 12:30.540
Oh.

12:31.210 --> 12:33.500
You were listening to music.

12:34.540 --> 12:35.880
Sorry for disturbing you.

12:35.880 --> 12:38.080
Don't mind me.

12:39.420 --> 12:41.080
Do you wanna listen too?

12:41.580 --> 12:42.670
Here's an earbud.

12:43.080 --> 12:44.420
No, that's okay.

12:45.130 --> 12:46.420
Well...

12:49.000 --> 12:52.500
I'm not asking what you want.

12:53.670 --> 12:55.290
K..Kubo-san!

12:57.290 --> 12:59.580
Alrighty! Shiraishi-kun, scooch over a bit.

13:01.380 --> 13:03.540
Let me sit on one half of your chair.

13:03.540 --> 13:05.380
Huh, uh...

13:11.080 --> 13:12.540
Now, let's listen.

13:12.960 --> 13:14.750
O-okay.

13:14.920 --> 13:16.210
<b>Blessing for Us Both</b>

14:06.250 --> 14:12.250
<b>Blessing for Us Both</b>

14:15.250 --> 14:16.460
It's over.

14:17.540 --> 14:19.630
Um, thanks for le-

14:20.130 --> 14:21.170
We're not done yet.

14:23.000 --> 14:25.960
I'm interested in the next song.

14:34.000 --> 14:36.880
Kubo-san, is the song playing?

14:37.250 --> 14:39.830
Nope, it hasn't started yet.

14:41.920 --> 14:43.330
All right, Shiraishi-kun.

14:43.920 --> 14:44.960
Um?

14:46.580 --> 14:49.330
I want to listen to the music you like.

14:50.830 --> 14:52.670
I don't have any good songs on my phone though!

14:53.170 --> 14:54.710
What kind of songs do you have on it?

14:55.790 --> 14:58.460
Songs from, like, anime and video games.

14:58.960 --> 15:01.670
I don't think you'd know any of them.

15:03.250 --> 15:04.290
Shiraishi-kun.

15:06.130 --> 15:08.130
It's because I don't know them that I'm asking.

15:09.460 --> 15:11.040
So let me listen to them.

15:12.500 --> 15:13.420
Okay then...

15:26.080 --> 15:27.790
What song is this?

15:28.210 --> 15:30.920
You know the manga I leant you the other day?

15:31.540 --> 15:36.130
That manga was made into an anime series,
and this is a song in the anime.

15:36.330 --> 15:40.670
Oh, really? That manga was enjoyable.

15:41.790 --> 15:46.420
You really think that? They're also making a film
adaptation actually, and I'm super hyped for it.

15:46.880 --> 15:53.710
The anime is faithful to the manga, the action is
especially amazing, and the animation is beautiful!

15:53.710 --> 15:54.630
Gotcha.

15:55.380 --> 15:58.750
And this song plays when
the main character's special move...

16:02.130 --> 16:03.080
Damn it!

16:04.960 --> 16:06.290
...end here?

16:07.040 --> 16:09.630
I definitely won't lose!

16:09.130 --> 16:10.420
Whatcha watching?

16:10.420 --> 16:11.580
I swear I won't lose!

16:11.580 --> 16:12.630
One second.

16:11.580 --> 16:12.630
I have no choice but to...

16:20.330 --> 16:22.330
This is what you're watching?

16:21.250 --> 16:25.790
At this rate... There's one thing I still haven't tried.

16:23.080 --> 16:25.500
My friends were talking about it.

16:26.170 --> 16:29.460
Hmm. Your friends, huh?

16:29.130 --> 16:31.290
This legendary sword casts the strongest magic!

16:32.630 --> 16:36.330
Sword x Magic! Critical slash!

16:40.580 --> 16:45.460
Seeing my sister being so cute while drinking a beer
fresh out of the shower is something special!

16:58.580 --> 16:59.420
<b>Highly-anticipated</b>

16:58.580 --> 16:59.420
<b>film adaptation!!</b>

16:59.420 --> 17:01.920
Ah, I can't wait!

17:03.920 --> 17:06.000
It's still March.

17:06.330 --> 17:07.830
<b>White Day</b>

17:23.920 --> 17:25.330
White Day, huh?

17:26.540 --> 17:28.790
I'd like to give a return gift,

17:29.000 --> 17:31.670
but I don't know who gave it to me.

17:33.080 --> 17:35.380
Wait, is there a way to get it to her?

17:35.710 --> 17:36.210
Ah!

17:38.460 --> 17:41.080
Although I usually have no presence,

17:41.250 --> 17:45.710
falling is one way I can get noticed.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.960
Sir! Are you okay?

17:51.000 --> 17:52.130
I'm fine.

17:55.130 --> 17:56.250
I'll take this, please.

17:56.250 --> 17:56.790
Huh?

18:01.130 --> 18:03.250
I've bought a return gift,

18:03.670 --> 18:04.830
but now it's a matter of giving it.

18:14.000 --> 18:14.790
All right.

18:16.040 --> 18:17.460
Um, Kubo-san.

18:18.540 --> 18:19.960
Do you have a second?

18:20.250 --> 18:24.920
What? It's unlike you to start a conversation.

18:27.330 --> 18:28.830
Talking here would be fine,

18:29.210 --> 18:31.290
but is it okay if we go somewhere else?

18:35.330 --> 18:37.460
So seriously, what's up?

18:38.380 --> 18:39.830
Um, so...

18:41.170 --> 18:43.380
I-it's about this.

18:46.040 --> 18:46.920
Sweets?

18:47.380 --> 18:49.380
Today's White Day.

18:49.710 --> 18:51.670
Really? Oh, yeah!

18:52.130 --> 18:53.960
Yeah. So,

18:54.460 --> 18:56.960
there's someone I want to give them to.

18:59.500 --> 19:00.460
Kubo-san?

19:03.790 --> 19:07.790
Um, who do you want to give them to?
A girl in our class?

19:07.920 --> 19:09.380
Or someone in another class?

19:09.710 --> 19:11.000
I don't know.

19:12.170 --> 19:12.920
Huh?

19:14.250 --> 19:17.790
I actually don't know who gave me a gift.

19:17.920 --> 19:20.330
But it was delicious.

19:20.670 --> 19:23.330
I think it was obligation chocolate, but I, uh...

19:23.330 --> 19:25.920
I want to make sure to give a return gift.

19:26.290 --> 19:30.210
Kubo-san, it seems like you know who gave it to me, so...

19:31.790 --> 19:35.000
How many Valentine's Day gifts did you get?

19:35.000 --> 19:35.710
Huh?

19:36.500 --> 19:40.250
One, but she put it in my desk.

19:42.670 --> 19:44.960
One. One, huh?

19:46.460 --> 19:47.830
Okay, I got it.

19:47.830 --> 19:49.420
Huh, what?

19:49.580 --> 19:53.130
Your Valentine's Day cookie was delicious.

19:54.420 --> 19:55.880
Y-yeah.

19:57.210 --> 20:02.210
We didn't need to go to the trouble of going
to another place just to pass this gift along.

20:02.880 --> 20:07.000
No one would've noticed you
if we did this in the classroom.

20:08.210 --> 20:09.170
True.

20:10.920 --> 20:14.790
Still, even though I know I'm invisible,

20:15.290 --> 20:18.380
doing this in the classroom would have felt odd.

20:19.210 --> 20:20.670
I'm not sure why.

20:20.670 --> 20:22.000
Aww.

20:22.000 --> 20:24.420
You said you wanted to go somewhere else, so...

20:27.750 --> 20:30.130
I thought you were gonna ask me out.

20:30.750 --> 20:31.960
Ask o-

20:34.920 --> 20:37.040
Th... Tha, tha, tha...

20:37.290 --> 20:38.960
Tha, tha, tha, tha...

20:38.960 --> 20:39.790
That's... That's...

20:39.790 --> 20:41.380
I'm joking!

20:41.380 --> 20:44.040
Shiraishi-kun, let's go back.

20:45.630 --> 20:48.040
I'll get this to her safe and sound for you, m'kay?

20:48.500 --> 20:53.420
Th-thank you. I hope she likes it.

20:54.000 --> 20:56.290
It's perfect. I like sweet things.

20:56.460 --> 20:57.080
Okay.

20:57.750 --> 21:00.330
It doesn't matter if Kubo-san likes it or not.

21:01.130 --> 21:01.830
Hmm?

21:03.750 --> 21:06.250
She's in an awfully good mood.

21:06.250 --> 21:07.130
What's wrong?

21:07.960 --> 21:08.750
Um,

21:09.290 --> 21:13.170
if you could tell me who gave me the cookie...

21:14.830 --> 21:15.830
Nagisa Kubo.

21:20.080 --> 21:20.880
Huh?

21:22.920 --> 21:24.380
If...

21:26.000 --> 21:26.710
If?

21:28.880 --> 21:31.330
If you got a Valentine's gift from her,
would you be happy?

21:36.040 --> 21:39.080
Wouldn't anyone be happy to get a gift from you?

21:40.830 --> 21:45.420
Well, class is about to start, so let's head back.

21:46.500 --> 21:47.080
Oh!

21:48.080 --> 21:51.210
Kubo-san, you never answered my question.

21:51.750 --> 21:55.670
That's all I'm saying.
If you don't know who it is, it's your fault!

21:55.670 --> 21:57.540
Huh, it's my fault?

21:59.460 --> 22:01.250
My fault?

22:11.080 --> 22:14.460
The school's shadow glows a dark red

22:14.460 --> 22:20.750
I haven't reached the end of my youth

22:21.000 --> 22:26.170
I've experienced a little bit of it, but it'll be over soon

22:26.170 --> 22:30.420
Along with the smiles you give me

22:30.420 --> 22:32.330
It's beautiful

22:32.330 --> 22:35.170
Is it okay to call this a miracle?

22:35.420 --> 22:41.080
I love, love, love these days

22:41.080 --> 22:47.540
But they won't last forever, so I tightly hold on to them

22:47.540 --> 22:51.670
Because we're kids and our spring has just begun

22:51.670 --> 22:55.040
Let's move forward, forward, forward, one step at a time

22:55.040 --> 22:58.380
Now, a firm wind faintly blows

22:58.380 --> 23:06.040
I hope our time together at least colors the world a little

23:06.040 --> 23:10.670
What kind of canvas will we paint? What kind of future will we have?

23:10.670 --> 23:14.460
I don't know, but I want to believe

23:13.750 --> 23:18.040
We'll definitely smile and wave at each other

23:14.830 --> 23:17.880
We look forward to tomorrow a little

23:17.880 --> 23:21.580
When we say, "See you later" to each other

23:21.670 --> 23:28.540
With the season's quick passing, our words repeat

23:28.540 --> 23:34.960
